        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "638d1fda-32eb-542a-afca-5580a2fce6ac",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alec Guinness, David Lean, Santha Rama Rau, E. M. Forster\n- Films: Great Expectations, Oliver Twist, The Bridge on the River Kwai, Lawrence of Arabia, Doctor Zhivago, A Passage to India\n- Roles: Herbert Pocket, Fagin, Col. Nicholson, Prince Faisal, General Yevgraf Zhivago, Professor Godbole\n- Works: A Passage to India\n\nFacts:\n- Alec Guinness collaborated with David Lean on Great Expectations (1946), playing Herbert Pocket.\n- Alec Guinness collaborated with David Lean on Oliver Twist (1948), playing Fagin.\n- Alec Guinness collaborated with David Lean on The Bridge on the River Kwai (1957), playing Col. Nicholson, and he won the Academy Award for Best Actor for that role.\n- Alec Guinness collaborated with David Lean on Lawrence of Arabia (1962), playing Prince Faisal.\n- Alec Guinness collaborated with David Lean on Doctor Zhivago (1965), playing General Yevgraf Zhivago.\n- Alec Guinness collaborated with David Lean on A Passage to India (1984), playing Professor Godbole.\n- The screenplay of A Passage to India was based on the play A Passage to India by Santha Rama Rau.\n- Santha Rama Rau's play A Passage to India was based on the novel A Passage to India by E. M. Forster.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "fb9abb98-7109-5422-9fb4-21f4c6b88db7",
        "text": "Page: Alec Guinness. Sentence: He is also known for his six collaborations with David Lean: Herbert Pocket in \"Great Expectations\" (1946), Fagin in \"Oliver Twist\" (1948), Col. Nicholson in \"The Bridge on the River Kwai\" (1957, for which he won the Academy Award for Best Actor), Prince Faisal in \"Lawrence of Arabia\" (1962), General Yevgraf Zhivago in \"Doctor Zhivago\" (1965), and Professor Godbole in \"A Passage to India\" (1984).\nPage: A Passage to India (film). Sentence: The screenplay is based on the play of the same name by Santha Rama Rau, which was based on the novel of the same name by E.M. Forster.",
